  "summary_en": "French text of the UNESCO Recommendation on the Ethics of AI, adopted in November 2021. It sets human-rights-based values, ten principles and policy action areas for member states, covering oversight, impact assessment, certification, data, environment, education and gender. It is general AI with no robot-specific provisions.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Values and principles centred on human dignity, human rights, environment and diversity",
   "Member states encouraged to adopt soft governance such as certification of AI systems with mutual recognition",
   "Ethical impact assessments, audits and independent AI ethics officers",
   "Human oversight and accountability must remain with humans; prohibits social scoring and mass surveillance uses",
   "Policy action areas include data, environment, gender, education, labour and health"
